WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.189 align:start position:0%
 
for more than  three months the burmese army has been  bombing  and shelling myanmar's current state  these latest attacks  after the coup it's bad and it could get  worse  have fled their homes due to air strikes  and fighting the free burma rangers is a  humanitarian  movement and organization we are not a  militia we're not part of any of the  armed groups  we are also not pacifists we believe  people have the right to defend their  own lives that's a basic human right  and to defend others karen state is  located in  south eastern myanmar on the border with  thailand  many people living there are now  desperate for aid  this is free burma ranger's account of a  recent mission  most places we work in burma you have to  walk and  it involves river crossings and walking  up and down mountains  we move with everything on our backs or  sometimes with attack animals as well  jets over our head right now i thought  marie bombed earlier today  can hear it day and night  they're on high alert for bombing and  soldiers  here we are in the little bunker i can  hear the aircraft right over us  flying around  and go mommy's reinforcing up this road  so we are  finding another way through with all  these supplies  30 of our rangers have been killed in  service  and those ranges that were caught by the  burma army if they were alive  they were tortured to death and killed  every one of them and so if we were  captured  we could expect death in some areas  rebel groups give them safe passage  don't pass that guy that land mine past  him  we were very close to a burma army camp  and so the local resistance  scouted the road out so that we could  cross this road  safely almost 50 000  people in the states have been displaced  by the fighting  in recent months their villages  are no longer safe this school was  bombed  you see the damage here all the kids  have run away now  this is piece of shrapnel from the  missile that came in  this damage here and there's shrapnel  everywhere  looks like secondary explosions like a  possible cluster bomb just the way  the dispersion and the kind of small  rounds that went in  the damage here school all these school  supplies  and kids notebooks  of the world  all the school supplies the trophies  from different sports and then all this  destruction  koren's ethnic armed forces have been  battling government soldiers for more  than  70 years but violence has surged  since the military seized power in  february  with ginter troops launching air and  ground attacks  this is the blood of a man who was  killed in here  by the airstrike he was wounded he  picked up his son who was injured  came down the stairs this is all his  blood  and took his son to his wife who was in  the trench  gave him to his wife and he died  conditions are very hard some of them  lost family members to the air strikes  or ground attacks  many of them are sick and there's no  school  they're hiding in the jungle now it's a  rainy season so it's psychologically  hard it's emotionally very hard and  physically it's hard  and sicknesses rise in these  circumstances  coming up to the families this place for  the bombing  people are hiding up here in the  mountains from burma army airstrikes  in this spot there are five families  among them the young mother whose  husband died  saving their son from the airstrikes  that child has already shrapnel still in  his head and his neck we couldn't get it  all out  so it makes you feel very sad and very  angry and it's wrong  sky news isn't allowed into myanmar to  verify  all of the stories you've heard we asked  myanmar's military for a comment  it hasn't responded  the burmese army has previously accused  free burma rangers of training and  assisting armed rebels  the group insists their focus is helping  those  in need our teams go to give help hope  and love and not to fight  however they can defend the people  they're with  how did we get involved here we were  invited by people in burma saying please  come and help us  and as long as the people want us  however long that takes we're in  all the way  allah

